# React / Next.js Rules

## Project Structure (src/)

```zsh
src/
├── app/              # Thin route files only (page.tsx, layout.tsx, route.ts)
│   ├── api/          # Route handlers
│   └── [route]/page.tsx
├── ui/               # Reusable UI primitives and shadcn components
│   ├── shadcn/       # Generated shadcn/ui components (never import directly)
│   ├── icons/        # Icon definitions
│   ├── providers/    # ThemeRegistry, FontProvider, etc.
│   └── index.ts      # Public API — always import from @/ui
├── ui-theme/         # Legacy MUI theme (scheduled for removal)
├── features/         # Feature components with business logic
│   ├── [feature]/    # Feature folder with index.ts barrel
│   └── index.ts      # Public API — always import from @/features
├── alerts/           # Alert system
├── config/           # Metadata, constants
└── lib/              # Utilities, DB, auth, validations
```

## App Router

- Pages: `src/app/[route]/page.tsx` — thin wrappers importing from `@/features`
- Layouts: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- API: `src/app/api/[route]/route.ts`

## Server vs Client Components

Default: Server Components. See `.cursor/rules/use-client.mdc` for the full decision procedure on `'use client'` placement.

Key points:

- Files in barrel exports that use hooks → add `'use client'`
- Internal files only imported from `'use client'` parents → no directive needed
- Never add `'use client'` to barrel files (`index.ts`) themselves

## Data & State

| Type        | Use                          |
|-------------|------------------------------|
| Server data | Server Components, Suspense  |
| Global      | Effector                     |
| URL         | searchParams                 |
| Local UI    | useState / useReducer        |

## Server Actions

- For mutations (create, update, delete)
- Validate input with Zod
- Return unified Result type
- Handle errors gracefully

## proxy.ts (not middleware.ts)

Next.js deprecated `middleware.ts`. Use `proxy.ts` instead:

- File: `src/proxy.ts`
- Export: `proxy(request)`, not `middleware`
- Use for: auth redirects, rate limiting, security headers

## Barrel Files & Imports

- Every reusable module has `index.ts` as its public API
- Import from barrels: `import { X } from '@/ui'` and `import { Y } from '@/features'`
- Never import directly from `@/ui/shadcn/` — use `@/ui` barrel
- Barrel files export only the public API — see `.cursor/rules/use-client.mdc` for barrel hygiene rules
